===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hemlok}}, {{m|enm|hemeluc}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hemlīc}}, {{m|ang|hymlīc|g=m}} and {{m|ang|hymlīce|g=f|t=hemlock, [[bryony]], [[convolvulus]]}}, of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. 
{{rel-top|speculative etymology}}
Compare {{m+|ang|hymele|t=hop-vine, hops}}, {{m+|ang|humele|t=bryony, widerton, hair moss, gold-hair, morning glory}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|sv|humle|t=hops}}, {{cog|is|humall|t=hops}}. Perhaps from {{der|en|xsc}}, from {{der|en|ira-pro|*háwHmah||[[ephedra]]; juice}}, from {{der|en|iir-pro|*sáwHmas}} from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sewh₁-||to press out, extract}}.
;cognates
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *haumala}} {{cog|os|хумӕллӕг||hops}}
* {{qualifier|from Sarmato-Scythian *hauma}} {{cog|ae|𐬵𐬀𐬊𐬨𐬀}}, {{cog|bal|tr=hum}}, {{cog|fa|هوم|tr=hōm}})
* {{qualifier|from Proto-Indo-Iranian *sauma}} {{cog|sa|सोम}})
More at [[suck]].
{{rel-bottom}}

